        "original_id": "d3e9e62a-8065-55b0-abfb-458591288f2a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tim Rice, Kathy Acker, Elton John, Hans Zimmer, Tonino Accolla, Kenneth Branagh, Tom Hanks, Mickey Rourke, Ralph Fiennes, Jim Carrey, Ben Stiller, Gary Oldman\n- Works: The Lion King, Léon, The Fifth Element\n- Roles: lyricist, composer, novelist, poet, playwright, essayist, dub actor, voice actor\n- Awards: Academy Award, Golden Globe Award, Tony Award, Grammy Award\n\nFacts:\n- Tim Rice was born on 10 November 1944 and is an English author and lyricist.\n- Tim Rice won Academy, Golden Globe, Tony, and Grammy awards.\n- Kathy Acker was born on April 18, 1944, and died on November 30, 1997.\n- Kathy Acker was an American experimental novelist, punk poet, playwright, essayist, postmodernist, and sex-positive feminist writer.\n- The Lion King original songs were written by composer Elton John and lyricist Tim Rice.\n- The Lion King original score was written by Hans Zimmer.\n- Tonino Accolla dubbed actors including Kenneth Branagh, Tom Hanks, Mickey Rourke, Ralph Fiennes, Jim Carrey, Ben Stiller, and Gary Oldman.\n- Tonino Accolla voiced Timon in the animated film The Lion King and dubbed Gary Oldman in Léon and The Fifth Element.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
